+From 036d755725854aa171a70c7a6d2f09fd0b787fb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Roman Kuraev <naoru.desu@gmail.com>
+Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:22:15 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: test external DSC on SM8250 (adapted from JS Deck
+ and Qualcomm)
+
+Carry the external DisplayPort DSC prototype adapted from JS Deck's
+Qualcomm-based work at:
+https://github.com/xzn/linux_msm/tree/eca1b90b558433fe1e28d9fa804f6ec466fa28b2
+
+Wire sink DSC/FEC capabilities, mode selection, DPU DSC resources, PPS
+transmission and compressed transfer-unit calculations together. The
+SM8250 adaptation uses DSC 1.1 and adds the dp_prefer_dsc test preference
+and source/sink state reporting in dp_debug.
+
+This is the unchanged driver diff from the integration r88 experiment.
+On the ASUS PG32UCDMR, 3840x2160 at 103 Hz worked at 10 bpc with DSC/FEC
+enabled, including a brief HDR check. Compressed 1080p at 240 Hz underruns,
+1440p at 231 Hz fails to start, and returning to uncompressed output can
+leave underruns until reboot. Keep this experimental; it does not raise
+the display engine's pixel-clock limit.
+
+The dp_prefer_dsc parameter defaults to false and is sampled on modeset.
+It prefers compression when optional; it is not a global DSC disable
+switch, since the mode policy can still select DSC when needed.
